            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "That is not really a bug: built-in Neovim (and Vim) completion behaves the same way. As 'mini.completion' is designed to use built-in mechanisms as much as possible, this can indeed be solved only by remapping `<CR>` in Insert mode. In turn, this is a very popular key for mapping in Insert, so early on I decided to not make any such mappings inside plugin.\r\n\r\nWhat I think is more appropriate here, is to document common code snippets used for making these mappings. I did so for `<Tab>` and `<S-Tab>`, but forgot for `<CR>`. So thank you for reminder!",
